## What it does

Food creators post recipes on Instagram and TikTok but rarely have a website. With Post2Plate, a creator shares or DMs a post, AI parses it, and it's published at `/@handle/recipe`, where fans can actually cook from it. The creator owns the audience.

I built it solo: product, brand (including Miso, the mascot), a FastAPI and Postgres backend, a Next.js front end and a Figma plugin.

## The AI

- **Parser:** gpt-oss-120b on Cerebras, with GPT-4o as fallback, at 92% on a 60-case test set. Video audio is transcribed with Whisper.
- **Intelligence heads:** I trained about ten small TF-IDF and logistic-regression models for tasks like ingredient substitution and canonicalization, labeled with larger LLMs. Some looked great (0.99 on canonicalization), but my own training journal later flagged a few of those wins as inflated, which was the most useful lesson of the project.
